course: dictionary
lesson: 14451
title: Paramecia: tiny one-celled swimmers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Paramecia is the plural word, so use it when you mean more than one. One tiny living thing is a paramecium. «Under the microscope, Sam could see three paramecia swimming in the pond water.» The word paramecia tells you that Sam saw more than one.
explain: A paramecium is a living thing so small you need a microscope to see it. It is made of just one cell, while you are made of many cells. «Each paramecium is only one cell, but it can still find food, move and grow.» Even one cell can do the jobs of a whole living thing.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «The paramecia wriggled through the water, beating their tiny cilia like little oars.» Cilia are tiny hairs, and they help the paramecia swim. When you meet a new science word, ask what it does in the sentence.
fact: Paramecia is the plural of paramecium: one paramecium, many paramecia.
fact: A paramecium is a tiny living thing made of only one cell.
fact: Paramecia live in fresh water, such as ponds.
fact: They are shaped like a slipper.
fact: They swim using tiny hairs called cilia.
exercise: «Mia saw three paramecia in the pond water.» How many paramecia did Mia see? | None at all | One | Thirty | *Three
exercise: A paramecium is made of how many cells? | Hundreds | Millions | Two | *One
exercise: How does a paramecium swim? | By flying with wings | *By beating tiny hairs called cilia | By wriggling like a snake | By sinking to the bottom
test: Where do paramecia live? | *In fresh water, such as ponds | Inside the sky | In salt sea water only | In hot deserts
test: What shape are paramecia? | Long like a snake | *Like a slipper | Round like a ball | Square like a box
exam: Which statement about paramecia is true? | They are huge animals that live in the sea | *They are tiny one-celled living things that live in fresh water | They are made of millions of cells | They have wings and fly through the air
